    "Description": "The kernel-rt packages provide the Real Time Linux Kernel, which enables fine-tuning for systems with extremely high determinism requirements.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: out-of-bound read in memcpy_fromiovecend() (CVE-2018-16885)\n\n* kernel: sctp: avoid NULL dereference when chunk data buffer is missing (CVE-2025-40240)\n\n* kernel: ALSA: aloop: Fix racy access at PCM trigger (CVE-2026-23191)\n\n* kernel: nfsd: fix heap overflow in NFSv4.0 LOCK replay cache (CVE-2026-31402)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
